# Append-only logs and the verification check tables: concurrent PRs each add an
# entry at the same spot, which is a textual conflict but never a real one. A
# union merge keeps both sides' lines. GitHub's own merge and "Update branch"
# ignore merge drivers, so this takes effect in local merges -- in particular
# `task pr:refresh`, which merges with the base branch's attributes, re-resolves
# each union hunk so a line one side edited is not kept twice beside its stale
# original, and lists every union-resolved file for review. A plain local
# `git merge` keeps both whole sides: check for a duplicated row by hand.
docs/project_notes/bugs.md merge=union
docs/project_notes/issues.md merge=union
docs/runbooks/verification.md merge=union
